{"type":"text","timestamp":1794539664665,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1e0418ffeDytqb0MDvpCbVu","part":{"id":"prt_1d2e621c7001vN7NTHitQCsQiJ","sessionID":"ses_e2d1e0418ffeDytqb0MDvpCbVu","messageID":"msg_1d2e6140a001ADUdFG9222gzlZ","type":"text","text":"T003 complete. Both verify runs were executed from the final state.\n\n## Files written\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` | `renderCommandRows` now builds a third map over every entry (no enabled filter), keyed by `entryRunnable(entry)`, throwing `[command-bridges] Conflicting tracked command <runnable>` on an owner/policy conflict, and renders a sorted `TRACKED_COMMANDS` block after `COMMAND_POLICIES`. |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Added the `TrackedCommand` interface with its governing comment above the generated block. The `TRACKED_COMMANDS` block itself was produced by running `node $DB`, not edited by hand. |\n\n`git status` shows only those two files changed. `command-bridges.generated.json` came back byte-identical. Skipped `.py`/`projection.ts` are untouched.\n\n## Verify output\n\n```\n$ node $DB --check | jq -r .status\nfresh\n\n$ rg -c \"scorerRow: (true|false) \\},$\" $CA\n63\n\n$ rg -n \"'/create:goal': { policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false },\" $CA\n184:  '/create:goal': { policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false },\n\n$ rg -n \"'/speckit:resume': { policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true },\" $CA\n238:  '/speckit:resume': { policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true },\n\n$ npm run typecheck        # in ADV\nEXIT:0\n\n$ npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts   # in ADV\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\n     Tests  11 passed (11)\n\n$ git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts\n(no output)\n```\n\nEvery stated expectation is met: `fresh`, 63 ≥ 44 `scorerRow` lines, one line for each named key, typecheck 0, 0 failed tests, no diff on the Python advisor or projection.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The checkbox in `tasks.md` was not ticked, per instruction.\n- Nothing was committed, pushed, or otherwise touched in git.\n- The stale-dist warning is pre-existing environment noise. No build was required by this task line, and both the drift guard and typecheck read source, so it did not affect verification.\n- Nothing from the task line was left undone.","time":{"start":1794539659719,"end":1794539664665}}}
